---
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';
---
<EditorialPage title="Built around your buying team." eyebrow="Client partnerships" description="A useful manufacturing partnership starts with clear requirements, an agreed reference and a shared understanding of quality, quantities and delivery.">
<section class="cat-section"><div class="cat-wrap"><div class="option-grid">{[['Brands & retailers','Develop garment collections around your target customer, reference styles, sizing and artwork.'],['Merchandising teams','Bring specifications, colour splits, trims and packing details together in a clear commercial brief.'],['Quality & compliance teams','Share inspection, testing and documentation requirements early so the applicable arrangements can be reviewed.']].map(([title,text])=><article class="option-panel"><h2 class="!text-2xl">{title}</h2><p class="mt-4">{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="cat-section"><div class="cat-wrap cat-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start with actual work</p><h2>Let the garment lead the conversation.</h2><p class="mt-5 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">Explore our real sample collection to discuss construction, silhouette and finishing. Client references and any buyer-specific case information are shared through our team where appropriate.</p><div class="cat-actions"><a class="cat-button" href="/products/">Explore the collection ↗</a><a class="cat-button secondary" href="/case-studies/">Selected work</a></div></div><div class="option-panel"><h3>For a focused first discussion</h3><ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm"><li>Your tech pack or reference garment</li><li>Intended quantities and colour/size split</li><li>Material and branding requirements</li><li>Testing, documentation and destination</li><li>Your target delivery window</li></ul></div></div></section>
</EditorialPage>
